The export does not support the current one-cause summary. Tenant locale and booking form separate the merged reports into two distinct failures. The totals below use unique report IDs and were derived from the private export; report message bodies are not part of this page.

<ReportCoverage />

## What to track

1. **Shared parser:** day-first tenant dates are read month-first. This covers app, email, and booking-v2 form reports.
2. **Booking-v3 form:** the form displays MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants, then parses in the tenant's day-first order.

Classify by the tenant's configured locale and form version. The browser locale and intake tag are guesses and cross the two causes.

Two GitHub issues track these causes: [shared parser (#1, 379 reports)](https://github.com/robertziolkowski/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) and [booking-v3 hint (#2, 33 reports)](https://github.com/robertziolkowski/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Engineering update · 2026-10-05

- **Parser — fixed:** fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales. Issue [#1](https://github.com/robertziolkowski/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) is closed as done.
- **Booking-v3 hint — won't fix:** the booking-v3 form was retired. Issue [#2](https://github.com/robertziolkowski/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) is closed as not planned.

